GeanyControl Plugin
===================

Exposes a Unix domain socket at ~/.config/geany/geanycontrol.sock so that
external processes (shell scripts, the agent terminal, CI pipelines) can
drive the Geany UI programmatically.  Also registers GLib signals on
geany->object for zero-overhead in-process inter-plugin IPC.

Command Protocol
----------------

Each command is a single UTF-8 line.  The server replies ok or error: <reason>.

  open-file <path>                  Open file in editor
  close-file <path>                 Close named document
  save-file <path>                  Save named document
  save-all                          Save all unsaved documents
  scroll-to-line <path>:<line>      Open file and scroll to line (1-based)
  get-current-file                  Return path of currently active document
  list-open-files                   Return newline-separated list of open files
  activate-menu-item <label>        Activate Tools-menu item by label (case-insensitive)
  refresh                           Signal treebrowser to reload the file tree
  ping                              Liveness probe

CLI Helper
----------

Use the companion geany-ctrl script (requires socat):

  geany-ctrl save-all
  geany-ctrl open-file /path/to/file.c
  geany-ctrl scroll-to-line /path/to/file.c:42
  geany-ctrl refresh

Inter-Plugin IPC
----------------

Other plugins can emit signals on geany->object:

  geanycontrol-open-file          (gchar *path)
  geanycontrol-close-file         (gchar *path)
  geanycontrol-save-file          (gchar *path)
  geanycontrol-save-all           (no args)
  geanycontrol-scroll-to-line     (gchar *"path:line")
  geanycontrol-activate-menu-item (gchar *label)
  geanycontrol-refresh            (no args)

Requirements
------------

  * Geany >= 2.1
  * socat (runtime, for geany-ctrl script only)

